    "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes the first-viewport corruption revealed by ADR-029's visual verification: `#p-lang-btn` (140-item \"In other languages\" dropdown) was rendering its children as visible blocks in the flow, consuming 4766px and pushing the article title to y=2470.\n\n**Root cause:** `#p-lang-btn` is a `:checked` / `position: absolute` dropdown in real Wikipedia — visible only on hover/click. Without those features (ADR-030 territory), all 140 `<li>` children render inline.\n\n## The two-stage measurement\n\n`.mw-page-container-inner` and article containers on Wikipedia at viewport 1774:\n\n| Element | Before workaround | After workaround | Delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `#p-lang-btn` | y=107, h=4766 | **display: none** | hidden |\n| `h1#firstHeading` | y=2470 | **y=107** | −2363 |\n| `vector-page-toolbar` | y=4873 | y=147 | −4726 |\n| `vector-body` (article) | y=5560 | **y=834** | −4726 |\n| Total layout height | 60612 | 55885 | −4727 |\n\n**Article title above the fold.** The PNG confirms it: \"HTML\" is the first large content element, with Article / Talk tabs, Read / View source / View history page actions, and \"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\" at the bottom edge.\n\n## What's still inline (ADR-030 work)\n\n**One more `:checked` dropdown remains visible**: `vector-page-toolbar` (the \"Tools\" panel, 687px) — same root cause as the language dropdown, but the `<li>` items are direct children of `.vector-dropdown` with no obvious wrapping class to hide surgically. Adding a second workaround risks fragility to Wikipedia's class names.\n\n**Deferred to ADR-030** (`:checked` + `position: absolute`): toolbar dropdown collapses properly, article intro moves above the fold (y=834 → y≈150).\n\n## What changed\n\n- `src/browser/render_pipeline.cpp` — `relayout()` injects `#p-lang-btn{display:none}` into `merged_css_` when `viewport_width >= 1120` (matches grid breakpoint)\n- `docs/decisions/029-flex-layout.md` — Post-Implementation Note updated to record the two-stage measurement and the remaining toolbar dropdown\n- `CHANGELOG.md` — entry documenting the workaround and the ADR-030 deferral\n- `tests/test_layout.cpp` — 2 new tests: `#p-lang-btn` hidden at desktop, not hidden at mobile\n\n## The discipline, applied twice in one cycle\n\nThis is the **second** time in ADR-029's short cycle the measure-verify-correct pattern caught an over-stated claim:\n\n1. **First catch** (mid-cycle): Commit 2 alone regressed +165px (header tall due to mobile menu). Commit 3 (feature-class flip) fixed it → −526px.\n2. **Second catch** (post-merge visual): grid at y=59 was correct, but the first viewport showed the language dropdown instead of the article. Small workaround → article title at y=107.\n\nNeither catch was a *regression* introduced by ADR-029 — both were the *discovery* of pre-existing CSS-feature gaps (JS-dependent class, `:checked`-dependent dropdown) that only became visible once the header was compact enough to expose the top of the article column. The arc's discipline worked: measure, note honestly, apply small workaround if defensible, defer principled fix to its own ADR.\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before: 392 cases / 1637 assertions\n- After: **394 cases / 1643 assertions** (+2 / +6)\n- Full suite all pass, zero warnings\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `#p-lang-btn` hidden at desktop (≥1120) | ✅ |\n| `#p-lang-btn` visible at mobile (<1120) | ✅ |\n| `h1#firstHeading` above fold at y=107 | ✅ |\n| Article title + tabs + page actions visible in first viewport | ✅ |\n| Page PNG shows \"HTML\" at top | ✅ |\n| No regression to flex layout, grid, prior ADRs | ✅ |\n| Full suite green (394 / 1643) | ✅ |\n\n## Deferred (ADR-030)\n\n- `:checked` pseudo-class support (language dropdown, page-tools dropdown, user menu)\n- `position: absolute` (dropdown positioning, infoboxes, thumbnails)\n- When both land, remove the `#p-lang-btn` workaround — the principled `:checked`-gated `display:none` will handle it\n\nRefs #164\n",
